  "caption": "Quinn spotted bowed legs in an old beach photo and spent three days trying to stretch them straight. The legs stayed curved, and the knees started to grumble.\n\nKay gave an honest answer: adult bone shape is set, and stretches can't reshape it. But exercise can work on how the legs feel and function, including pain, balance and strength.\n\nWhat can help: side-glute work like clamshells and side-lying leg lifts, quad and hamstring strength within comfort, progressive one-leg balance, and supportive shoes plus managing load.\n\nGet it checked if the bowing changes quickly, one leg is much worse, there's pain at rest or night, the knee gives way, or bowing appears after an injury.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
